# ripgrep, read via RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH (exported in zshenv — every rg
# with a shell ancestor, interactive or not; CLI flags override). One shell ARGUMENT per line,
# verbatim: no trailing comments (`--flag # c` is one unrecognised flag),
# no quotes (a quoted flag is read as the positional PATTERN and poisons
# the whole invocation), values via `--flag=value` only. Measured against
# rg 15.2.0.

# The same world every other searcher sees: GLOB_DOTS for `*`, fd
# --hidden --exclude .git for fzf. Hidden files yes, .git never.
--hidden
--glob=!.git

# Case folds until the pattern carries a capital — completion's
# case-insensitivity, applied to search.
--smart-case

# Matches open in the editor on click — the eza --hyperlink instinct.
# Emitted only on a real terminal, so pipes and captures stay clean.
--hyperlink-format=kitty
